WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:01.310
Alert!

00:00:01.310 --> 00:00:05.140
You are attempting to view the file on SCP-001.

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:10.520
This file is highly classified, and its contents
are sealed by the order of the O5 Council.

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:15.530
By continuing to view them, you are confirming
that you have received prior authorization.

00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:20.640
If you are found to be viewing these materials
without adequate clearance, you will be terminated.

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:25.619
If you choose to accept these risks, and verify
your credentials, access will be granted in

00:00:25.619 --> 00:00:29.429
5...4...3...2...1.

00:00:29.429 --> 00:00:33.730
The following is a truncated summary, based
on transcripts from an official meeting of

00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:35.230
the O5 Council.

00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:36.760
You have been warned.

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:40.980
O5-1 sat at a conference table, addressing
his colleagues.

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:45.030
All of the other council members looked at
him expectantly, except one.

00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:46.450
"Hello everyone."

00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:51.540
O5-1 began, "I'm sure you're all wondering
why Thirteen isn't here today.

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:56.210
I'll get to that, but first I want to publicly
address something I'm sure you've all noticed

00:00:56.210 --> 00:00:57.210
by now.

00:00:57.210 --> 00:01:01.210
After talking to you for the past week or
so, I've noticed that we've all been inducted

00:01:01.210 --> 00:01:04.530
onto the Council almost at the exact same
time.

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:07.350
All of us, except Thirteen that is.

00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:10.700
In fact, Thirteen probably conducted your
orientation."

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:12.280
The other council members nodded.

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:16.060
"It's good to know that wasn't just me," O5-2
commented.

00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:19.369
"I would've expected the last Two to run me
through things."

00:01:19.369 --> 00:01:20.450
O5-1 sighed.

00:01:20.450 --> 00:01:21.450
"Indeed.

00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:25.430
In fact, I asked Thirteen about it, but he
refused to say much.

00:01:25.430 --> 00:01:28.270
Of course, he pled ignorance, but I don't
believe that.

00:01:28.270 --> 00:01:32.159
As you might guess, the previous twelve O5s
did not retire at the same time.

00:01:32.159 --> 00:01:33.590
They were killed.

00:01:33.590 --> 00:01:38.219
In fact, this building isn't even the original
Site-01.

00:01:38.219 --> 00:01:39.219
That was destroyed.

00:01:39.219 --> 00:01:41.310
I think you can see where this is going."

00:01:41.310 --> 00:01:42.479
O5-3 frowned.

00:01:42.479 --> 00:01:49.080
"So, we have a dead O5 council, a missing
Site-01, and somehow none of this is on our

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:50.080
records."

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:54.200
"And only one suspect," piped up O5-2.

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:57.219
O5-1 held up a hand, drawing attention back
to his words.

00:01:57.219 --> 00:02:02.600
"I would like to designate O5-13 as one of
our SCP-001 projects.

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:07.329
Of course, this will be kept secret from him,
but we need to investigate this entire ordeal

00:02:07.329 --> 00:02:13.209
until we figure out what happened, how it
happened, and why O5-13 is the only one left

00:02:13.209 --> 00:02:14.230
standing."

00:02:14.230 --> 00:02:19.689
After the aforementioned conference, O5-13
was designated SCP-001.

00:02:19.689 --> 00:02:27.379
SCP-001 is a male human of Latin American
descent, standing at approximately 1.9m tall.

00:02:27.379 --> 00:02:32.540
The exact nature of this entity, and the anomalous
properties he possesses, are not yet known.

00:02:32.540 --> 00:02:36.819
He was given his anomalous classification
following the Caesar Incident, an event that

00:02:36.819 --> 00:02:42.860
resulted in the death of all previous O5 Council
members aside from 13, the complete eradication

00:02:42.860 --> 00:02:48.720
of the previous Site-01, and the loss of any
official documentation on 13 or his appointment

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:50.200
to the Council.

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:56.370
SCP-001 is contained in a modified containment
facility constructed similarly to other Foundation

00:02:56.370 --> 00:03:01.209
Sites, with the exception of additional living
arrangements for the members of the Overwatch

00:03:01.209 --> 00:03:02.209
Council.

00:03:02.209 --> 00:03:06.500
The facility is equipped with state-of-the-art
security cameras, as well as three nuclear

00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:08.629
warheads intended as fail safes.

00:03:08.629 --> 00:03:12.380
These will detonate if SCP-001 breaches containment.

00:03:12.380 --> 00:03:17.409
One designated member of the Council is to
be given mnestic drugs on a regular basis,

00:03:17.409 --> 00:03:22.989
and maintain official documentation of all
information gathered about SCP-001.

00:03:22.989 --> 00:03:27.360
This Council member will be referred to as
The Archivist and will hold the position for

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:31.730
approximately four months at a time, though
they may terminate their duties sooner if

00:03:31.730 --> 00:03:34.939
the mnestics' side effects prove too detrimental
to their health.

00:03:34.939 --> 00:03:39.560
When a Council member's time as the Archivist
comes to a close, they must conduct a meeting

00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:41.530
to assess what they have learned.

00:03:41.530 --> 00:03:47.049
O5-1 was appointed to the role of inaugural
Archivist, and several months later, a second

00:03:47.049 --> 00:03:48.689
Conference was called.

00:03:48.689 --> 00:03:52.719
One of the subjects discussed was a series
of interviews conducted with survivors of

00:03:52.719 --> 00:03:54.080
the Caesar Incident.

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:58.189
Though several members of personnel made it
out relatively unscathed, they had no memory

00:03:58.189 --> 00:04:02.900
of the incident at all, and their interviews
were unfortunately of no help.

00:04:02.900 --> 00:04:07.830
During the events of the conference, O5-10
revealed that he had recovered a copy of the

00:04:07.830 --> 00:04:10.409
previous O5 Personnel Dossier.

00:04:10.409 --> 00:04:15.640
It included an entry that described O5-13's
purpose on the council, stating:

00:04:15.640 --> 00:04:20.549
"O5-13's special connection to the anomalous
gives him a perspective no other council member

00:04:20.549 --> 00:04:22.130
could begin to fathom.

00:04:22.130 --> 00:04:26.840
While Normalcy Confirmation meetings require
eleven members for quorum, no meeting is allowed

00:04:26.840 --> 00:04:30.430
to proceed without O5-13's attendance."

00:04:30.430 --> 00:04:35.900
In addition to this entry, there was a table
recording O5-13's various Anomalous Property

00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:36.900
Measurements.

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:42.610
Perplexingly, his appearance, temperature,
skeletal structure, corporeality, and induced

00:04:42.610 --> 00:04:46.400
emotional states were all found to be within
the baseline of normality.

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:50.450
The remainder of the conference was dedicated
to deciding the next steps for a series of

00:04:50.450 --> 00:04:56.990
specialized teams looking into the Caesar
Incident, SCP-001's Origin, and the entity's

00:04:56.990 --> 00:04:58.690
anomalous properties.

00:04:58.690 --> 00:05:03.610
O5-8 was selected as the next Archivist, and
the meeting disbanded with a new sense of

00:05:03.610 --> 00:05:04.610
purpose.

00:05:04.610 --> 00:05:08.490
The Caesar Incident Team managed to identify
the geographical location of the previous

00:05:08.490 --> 00:05:14.199
Site-01 by searching for records of unusual
seismic activity on the date of the incident.

00:05:14.199 --> 00:05:18.470
Earthquake records led them to an island off
the coast of Greenland, where the remains

00:05:18.470 --> 00:05:19.960
of the Site were waiting.

00:05:19.960 --> 00:05:24.020
An investigative team attempted to search
the island, but was prevented from exploring

00:05:24.020 --> 00:05:28.570
the ruins by representatives of the Global
Occult Coalition, who demanded they leave

00:05:28.570 --> 00:05:30.120
immediately.

00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:34.660
Investigation into the presence of the GOC
on the island turned up a curious connection:

00:05:34.660 --> 00:05:39.770
their representatives had spoken with O5-13
before setting up an outpost there.

00:05:39.770 --> 00:05:44.880
Meanwhile, the Origins Investigation team
looked into records of O5-13 at various Groups

00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:45.990
of Interest.

00:05:45.990 --> 00:05:50.289
Reports were conflicting and difficult to
parse, and the team brought their findings

00:05:50.289 --> 00:05:52.320
to the third Conference.

00:05:52.320 --> 00:05:56.580
Notice from O5-8:
"Conference #3 was cut short after an intense

00:05:56.580 --> 00:06:00.660
exchange led to enough people leaving the
meeting for us to lose quorum.

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:04.880
We archived all of the material covered up
to that point, as well as the efforts made

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:07.390
to de-escalate tension between the members.

00:06:07.390 --> 00:06:11.389
However, this also means that information
herein was not properly vetted by the entire

00:06:11.389 --> 00:06:15.569
Council before being uploaded, so we erred
on the conservative side.

00:06:15.569 --> 00:06:19.110
If you need to see the full proceedings, please
contact the current Archivist."

00:06:19.110 --> 00:06:23.280
Before the premature adjourning of the conference,
the following conversation took place:

00:06:23.280 --> 00:06:25.140
O5-1: Excuse me, Four.

00:06:25.140 --> 00:06:28.879
I believe some clarification regarding the
exchange with Marshall, Carter, and Dark is

00:06:28.879 --> 00:06:29.879
necessary.

00:06:29.879 --> 00:06:30.879
O5-4: How so?

00:06:30.879 --> 00:06:33.050
O5-1: It mentions here that you performed
an exchange.

00:06:33.050 --> 00:06:37.069
It is important for the records, and for our
general information security that we know

00:06:37.069 --> 00:06:39.550
exactly what information was exchanged.

00:06:39.550 --> 00:06:41.110
O5-4: Yes, that does make sense.

00:06:41.110 --> 00:06:43.730
I'm sorry, I did not write that section of
the report.

00:06:43.730 --> 00:06:48.539
O5-10: If my memory serves me well, Seven
was responsible for the Marshall, Carter,

00:06:48.539 --> 00:06:49.550
and Dark reconnaissance.

00:06:49.550 --> 00:06:52.259
O5-1: Well, Seven, could you elaborate?

00:06:52.259 --> 00:06:54.470
O5-7 looked at O5-1 and swallowed.

00:06:54.470 --> 00:06:56.789
O5-11: You know, the rules are pretty tight
on this.

00:06:56.789 --> 00:06:59.330
Why did you give them anything in the first
place?

00:06:59.330 --> 00:07:01.800
O5-3: Eleven makes a good point.

00:07:01.800 --> 00:07:05.300
Don't we have our own spies working some of
the transport routes?

00:07:05.300 --> 00:07:08.009
O5-7 nodded and then began going through her
belongings.

00:07:08.009 --> 00:07:12.500
O5-3: Could you at least tell us what kind
of information you gave them?

00:07:12.500 --> 00:07:16.819
O5-7 paused, thought to herself for a moment,
and then motioned to the entire Council.

00:07:16.819 --> 00:07:20.370
O5-11: Wait, you gave them information about
us?

00:07:20.370 --> 00:07:25.070
O5-7 shook her head, paused again, and then
nodded her head yes.

00:07:25.070 --> 00:07:28.479
She held up a finger and then went back to
looking through her files.

00:07:28.479 --> 00:07:30.219
O5-11: But that's— No.

00:07:30.219 --> 00:07:31.670
I don't believe this.

00:07:31.670 --> 00:07:34.539
We can't let people know about us no matter
the situation.

00:07:34.539 --> 00:07:37.319
Imagine if word got out that the old Council
had been killed.

00:07:37.319 --> 00:07:39.620
I bet cults across the planet would have a
hay day.

00:07:39.620 --> 00:07:42.370
O5-4: I doubt that she said anything actually
important.

00:07:42.370 --> 00:07:43.600
O5-11: Oh really?

00:07:43.600 --> 00:07:47.720
I've only dealt with the merchants once or
twice, but they know how to appraise anything,

00:07:47.720 --> 00:07:49.340
especially information.

00:07:49.340 --> 00:07:53.470
O5-7 held up an index finger and then continued
looking through her files.

00:07:53.470 --> 00:07:56.139
O5-11: Are you just going to ignore the issue
then?

00:07:56.139 --> 00:07:57.810
Just going to hang us out to dry?

00:07:57.810 --> 00:07:59.220
O5-8: Eleven, you need to calm down.

00:07:59.220 --> 00:08:01.000
O5-11: We're all waiting on you.

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:02.150
[under his breath] Dumb bitch.

00:08:02.150 --> 00:08:05.490
O5-7 looked up at O5-11 and then put her files
away.

00:08:05.490 --> 00:08:07.810
She gathered her things and left the room.

00:08:07.810 --> 00:08:10.400
O5-11: Can't take being called out, I see.

00:08:10.400 --> 00:08:12.910
O5-1: Eleven, I will need to speak with you
following this meeting.

00:08:12.910 --> 00:08:14.250
O5-11: You can talk to me now.

00:08:14.250 --> 00:08:15.689
I'll be in my office.

00:08:15.689 --> 00:08:17.160
O5-11 left the room.

00:08:17.160 --> 00:08:21.069
O5-4: Eight, I'd like to go after Seven to
make sure she didn't actually do something

00:08:21.069 --> 00:08:22.069
stupid.

00:08:22.069 --> 00:08:23.069
O5-8: That's fine.

00:08:23.069 --> 00:08:26.080
I believe that would drop us below quorum,
but I believe this meeting has fallen apart

00:08:26.080 --> 00:08:27.080
anyway.

00:08:27.080 --> 00:08:29.699
One, Twelve, and I will make the next update
ourselves.

00:08:29.699 --> 00:08:32.659
This SCP-001 Conference is dismissed.

00:08:32.659 --> 00:08:33.659
Addendum.

00:08:33.659 --> 00:08:37.459
An update has been added to this file by O5-8,
regarding security concerns:

00:08:37.459 --> 00:08:42.640
"Following the official ending of the meeting,
O5-7 distributed the summary of all information

00:08:42.640 --> 00:08:45.110
exchanged with Marshall, Carter, and Dark.

00:08:45.110 --> 00:08:48.079
The information was pulled from the out-of-date
O5 Dossier.

00:08:48.079 --> 00:08:52.160
The current explanation as to why it was accepted
by the Group of Interest is that it would

00:08:52.160 --> 00:08:56.510
have confirmed any information they had gathered
previously about the O5 Council.

00:08:56.510 --> 00:09:00.440
As part of the exchange we have received a
tip as to where to find more information on

00:09:00.440 --> 00:09:05.880
SCP-001, which the Origins Team will investigate
for the next conference.

00:09:05.880 --> 00:09:10.029
O5-7 later clarified in a written statement
that she had left the meeting simply to retrieve

00:09:10.029 --> 00:09:14.149
the file detailing this information, since
it was not on her person.

00:09:14.149 --> 00:09:19.390
O5-7 insisted that she does not need an interpreter,
due to information security concerns.

00:09:19.390 --> 00:09:24.870
A discussion was scheduled between her and
O5-1 to reduce communicational issues at a

00:09:24.870 --> 00:09:26.149
later date.

00:09:26.149 --> 00:09:28.090
O5-11 issued a formal apology.

00:09:28.090 --> 00:09:31.730
I hope that this will be the cessation of
any internal conflicts.

00:09:31.730 --> 00:09:36.600
We are working together, and therefore require
that a trusting relationship has been established

00:09:36.600 --> 00:09:38.280
between all members.

00:09:38.280 --> 00:09:42.860
As Abraham Lincoln once said, "A house divided
against itself, cannot stand."

00:09:42.860 --> 00:09:48.550
O5-12 was appointed to the position of Archivist,
and after several months passed, a fourth

00:09:48.550 --> 00:09:50.029
conference was called.

00:09:50.029 --> 00:09:54.310
The following is an excerpt from this meeting:
O5-12: Two, why doesn't your team start us

00:09:54.310 --> 00:09:55.310
off.

00:09:55.310 --> 00:09:56.310
O5-2: Alright, sure.

00:09:56.310 --> 00:09:57.830
We did make some nice progress.

00:09:57.830 --> 00:09:59.750
O5-8: Always good to start a meeting on a
high note.

00:09:59.750 --> 00:10:03.100
O5-2: You all remember those four survivors
we talked about last meeting, right?

00:10:03.100 --> 00:10:06.440
We got back in touch with them and did a more…

00:10:06.440 --> 00:10:07.790
thorough interview.

00:10:07.790 --> 00:10:11.990
More intense techniques, lie detector tests,
heart rate monitoring, the whole shebang.

00:10:11.990 --> 00:10:13.400
O5-3: Do you have transcripts?

00:10:13.400 --> 00:10:17.990
O5-2: I do but, spoiler-alert, they're not
very different from the first round.

00:10:17.990 --> 00:10:21.400
O5-9: So, we're now convinced they genuinely
don't remember.

00:10:21.400 --> 00:10:24.200
O5-11: How far does Thirteen's antimemetic
side reach?

00:10:24.200 --> 00:10:25.200
O5-2: Slow down there.

00:10:25.200 --> 00:10:26.200
We're not quite done.

00:10:26.200 --> 00:10:29.860
You see, as part of our second round of interviews,
we also did a physical examination and some

00:10:29.860 --> 00:10:32.829
tests to see what messed with their heads.

00:10:32.829 --> 00:10:37.120
And we found they all had a little scar, right
on the side of their necks.

00:10:37.120 --> 00:10:38.340
Right where we inject amnestics.

00:10:38.340 --> 00:10:42.370
O5-8: I mean, while I understand what you're
implying, we tend to administer amnestics

00:10:42.370 --> 00:10:44.070
fairly liberally.

00:10:44.070 --> 00:10:47.480
Last meeting was essentially just a prolonged
reminder of how much we value InfoSec.

00:10:47.480 --> 00:10:52.130
O5-2: True, but we keep good records of who
we use with that stuff, how much we're using,

00:10:52.130 --> 00:10:54.600
if we're using the pills or the syringe, etcetera.

00:10:54.600 --> 00:10:59.529
However, when I went to look up if any of
our "survivors" had ever taken the injectable

00:10:59.529 --> 00:11:01.269
amnestic, all my results came back negative.

00:11:01.269 --> 00:11:04.230
O5-6: I also took the liberty of checking
out Red Right Hand.

00:11:04.230 --> 00:11:07.680
The entire squad's got injection scars, and
we rarely wipe those guys.

00:11:07.680 --> 00:11:08.950
O5-2: Whatever happened…

00:11:08.950 --> 00:11:11.750
I think we covered it up ourselves.

00:11:11.750 --> 00:11:18.680
O5-1: When you say "ourselves" do you mean—
O5-2: Oh, no I just mean the Foundation.

00:11:18.680 --> 00:11:22.410
If we were actually involved, then everyone
here would have those scars, but Six, Nine,

00:11:22.410 --> 00:11:26.670
and I definitely don't have them, so that
leads me to believe they didn't drug us.

00:11:26.670 --> 00:11:28.510
It would be an all-or-nothing deal.

00:11:28.510 --> 00:11:29.959
O5-12: Good work.

00:11:29.959 --> 00:11:32.589
Sounds like Eight needs to have a talk with
our Amnestics Department.

00:11:32.589 --> 00:11:34.130
O5-8: Wait, wait.

00:11:34.130 --> 00:11:36.410
Sorry, I'm still trying to keep all details
in order.

00:11:36.410 --> 00:11:38.089
You said they were injected?

00:11:38.089 --> 00:11:39.320
O5-2: Yeah.

00:11:39.320 --> 00:11:41.850
O5-8: See, that's what I don't get.

00:11:41.850 --> 00:11:44.090
We used the injections like, ten years ago?

00:11:44.090 --> 00:11:46.200
We moved onto the pills since you can miss
a vein.

00:11:46.200 --> 00:11:49.589
Also, I checked our amnestics supply right
after the Caesar event, and we didn't see

00:11:49.589 --> 00:11:51.610
any variation from our normal usage.

00:11:51.610 --> 00:11:53.320
O5-6: Maybe the records are off?

00:11:53.320 --> 00:11:56.579
We've found that whatever Thirteen did, he's
good at covering up his tracks.

00:11:56.579 --> 00:11:59.430
O5-8: I don't think that's it.

00:11:59.430 --> 00:12:03.070
Because you know who does still use those
injectable amnestics?

00:12:03.070 --> 00:12:04.070
The GOC.

00:12:04.070 --> 00:12:08.949
O5-12: I see we'll have to schedule another
meeting with our good friends at the UN as

00:12:08.949 --> 00:12:09.949
well.

00:12:09.949 --> 00:12:15.660
After discussing potential origins for SCP-001,
the Council moved on to the subject of O5-13's

00:12:15.660 --> 00:12:16.720
anomalous properties.

00:12:16.720 --> 00:12:18.870
The Anomalous Properties Team presented their
findings:

00:12:18.870 --> 00:12:23.510
O5-3: Ok… so everyone here has the records
of our measurements, although I can tell you

00:12:23.510 --> 00:12:25.740
now, they are not particularly insightful.

00:12:25.740 --> 00:12:29.700
O5-10: Do you have too many leads to choose
from?

00:12:29.700 --> 00:12:31.790
O5-5: Quite the opposite actually.

00:12:31.790 --> 00:12:33.320
We have nothing.

00:12:33.320 --> 00:12:36.889
Nothing abnormal with regard to radiation,
humes, radio frequencies.

00:12:36.889 --> 00:12:38.880
Thirteen is almost impressively normal.

00:12:38.880 --> 00:12:41.769
O5-2: Are you sure we're not going about this
wrong?

00:12:41.769 --> 00:12:46.160
I mean, I know we've kind of quantified some
of our anomalies in the past but, as a general

00:12:46.160 --> 00:12:48.660
rule they're not supposed to follow the rules,
right?

00:12:48.660 --> 00:12:53.550
O5-3: That is what I was beginning to suspect,
although it is troubling that he can just

00:12:53.550 --> 00:12:55.389
hide it from us entirely.

00:12:55.389 --> 00:12:59.880
O5-5: Or there's the other option - we're
not only barking up the wrong tree, but we're

00:12:59.880 --> 00:13:01.980
in the entirely wrong forest.

00:13:01.980 --> 00:13:04.990
O5-4: You saying he's not even anomalous in
the first place?

00:13:04.990 --> 00:13:08.269
O5-3: It's either that, or we're dealing with
a god.

00:13:08.269 --> 00:13:11.660
And a god who knows the Foundation better
than even we do.

00:13:11.660 --> 00:13:15.760
O5-1: Let's continue to discuss the non-anomalous
option, since it appears that there would

00:13:15.760 --> 00:13:18.630
be very little we could do about the other
case.

00:13:18.630 --> 00:13:22.970
O5-9: So, that would mean that he's probably
an inside man for the Insurgency.

00:13:22.970 --> 00:13:25.019
O5-11: Or Serpent's Hand.

00:13:25.019 --> 00:13:27.311
O5-3: No, not the hand.

00:13:27.311 --> 00:13:28.430
They don't operate like this.

00:13:28.430 --> 00:13:30.510
O5-2: He might be a Fifthist fanatic.

00:13:30.510 --> 00:13:31.760
O5-9: That too.

00:13:31.760 --> 00:13:34.279
O5-1: Or maybe he's with someone else.

00:13:34.279 --> 00:13:37.329
We've seen quite a bit of the GOC and UIU
popping up in this.

00:13:37.329 --> 00:13:41.020
O5-10: My apologies, but I do find it difficult
to believe that a single insurgent would be

00:13:41.020 --> 00:13:45.660
able to detonate the on-site nuclear warhead
from half-way across the globe, if we believe

00:13:45.660 --> 00:13:46.839
our previous information.

00:13:46.839 --> 00:13:49.649
O5-3: I'm not sure we can though.

00:13:49.649 --> 00:13:52.149
It sounds like he spoke to our regular body
double.

00:13:52.149 --> 00:13:55.089
O5-5: Maybe his anomalous property is that
he can create body doubles?

00:13:55.089 --> 00:13:57.450
O5-11: But what are we supposed to do with
that?

00:13:57.450 --> 00:14:00.959
O5-12: Excuse me, but I would like to return
to the earlier line of discussion about Thirteen

00:14:00.959 --> 00:14:04.720
being unable to perform the assassination
due to possibly meeting with our point of

00:14:04.720 --> 00:14:08.670
contact, because I am beginning to believe
that he actually did meet with Thirteen.

00:14:08.670 --> 00:14:13.230
O5-5: So, you believe that he was able to
blow Site-01 sky high from halfway across

00:14:13.230 --> 00:14:14.230
the globe?

00:14:14.230 --> 00:14:16.550
I mean, if we're going with the god theory
I could see it.

00:14:16.550 --> 00:14:18.649
O5-12: No, I'm saying he had help.

00:14:18.649 --> 00:14:21.130
Or at least more than one man helping him.

00:14:21.130 --> 00:14:24.440
Remember how our request to install additional
security cameras was denied by the Ethics

00:14:24.440 --> 00:14:25.440
Committee?

00:14:25.440 --> 00:14:26.440
O5-6: Did you finally talk to them?

00:14:26.440 --> 00:14:27.440
O5-12: I did.

00:14:27.440 --> 00:14:29.620
I met with Mr. Huang to demand an explanation.

00:14:29.620 --> 00:14:33.019
He refused and told me it was above my security
clearance.

00:14:33.019 --> 00:14:35.820
O5-11: Above your security clearance?

00:14:35.820 --> 00:14:39.810
You're on the Council, there simply aren't
things "outside of your jurisdiction".

00:14:39.810 --> 00:14:42.820
You run the Ethics Committee for goodness
sakes!

00:14:42.820 --> 00:14:44.800
O5-12: That's not quite accurate.

00:14:44.800 --> 00:14:49.320
I am not in charge of the Ethics Committee,
I'm simply the O5 ambassador to it.

00:14:49.320 --> 00:14:52.360
They need to be a separate entity to eliminate
bias in various cases.

00:14:52.360 --> 00:14:55.709
O5-1: So, you believe that Thirteen is in
league with the Ethics Committee?

00:14:55.709 --> 00:14:59.410
O5-3: Or the Administrator if it's set above
your security clearance.

00:14:59.410 --> 00:15:01.070
O5-12: Or both.

00:15:01.070 --> 00:15:04.750
Whoever it is, they are trying very hard to
stop us from seeing him in private.

00:15:04.750 --> 00:15:07.130
O5-11: Someone should just let us give him
a full physical.

00:15:07.130 --> 00:15:10.000
He's probably baseline, this would let us
confirm that.

00:15:10.000 --> 00:15:15.329
O5-2: Yeah, but if we're wrong and our "god
theory" is correct, he'll blow our asses sky-high

00:15:15.329 --> 00:15:16.889
like the last council.

00:15:16.889 --> 00:15:20.339
O5-1: I believe that we need to adjourn here,
so we have enough time to prepare for our

00:15:20.339 --> 00:15:22.610
next full Council meeting to avoid suspicion.

00:15:22.610 --> 00:15:25.160
Although we do need to expand our search further.

00:15:25.160 --> 00:15:29.670
I will consider speaking to Thirteen before
the next conference, but I will only do so

00:15:29.670 --> 00:15:32.450
if I believe it will not result in a second
Caesar Incident.

00:15:32.450 --> 00:15:35.060
Are there any objections to this?

00:15:35.060 --> 00:15:36.199
The council fell silent.

00:15:36.199 --> 00:15:38.540
O5-1: Then I believe this conference is dismissed.

00:15:38.540 --> 00:15:39.540
Alert!

00:15:39.540 --> 00:15:41.620
Retinal scan confirmed.

00:15:41.620 --> 00:15:42.850
Identity verified.

00:15:42.850 --> 00:15:46.860
Your credentials have been accepted, and further
access has been granted.

00:15:46.860 --> 00:15:49.110
Welcome, O5-13.

00:15:49.110 --> 00:15:51.779
You have one new message:
"Hello Thirteen,

00:15:51.779 --> 00:15:55.690
I’m sure you’ve been keeping tabs on your
fellow Council’s progress.

00:15:55.690 --> 00:16:00.199
They’re growing closer than either of us
wanted, but I’m not surprised.

00:16:00.199 --> 00:16:03.769
When you get enough smart people together,
they tend to surpass your expectations.

00:16:03.769 --> 00:16:06.460
You’re probably hoping this is going to
end soon.

00:16:06.460 --> 00:16:10.160
I’m sorry you’ve gone through this, it
obviously wasn’t in our plan for you when

00:16:10.160 --> 00:16:11.770
we inducted you into the council.

00:16:11.770 --> 00:16:16.350
But, if you could keep up our gambit a little
longer I would be appreciative.

00:16:16.350 --> 00:16:20.930
I’m unconvinced your cohorts are ready to
know what happened to their predecessors,

00:16:20.930 --> 00:16:25.420
and I don’t want to ask Al Fine and Johnson
to help clean up another May 13th.

00:16:25.420 --> 00:16:28.072
I don't even want the thought of pulling a
Caesar Event in their heads.

00:16:28.072 --> 00:16:33.269
The GOC and the UIU already have enough dangling
over my head as is.

00:16:33.269 --> 00:16:37.260
But if they do approach you, and confront
you about the situation, I’d rather you

00:16:37.260 --> 00:16:38.940
have a direct answer.

00:16:38.940 --> 00:16:41.500
Also, transcripts tend to be more convincing
than recall.

00:16:41.500 --> 00:16:45.649
I’ve attached here the transcript from the
O5 meeting before the "Caesar Incident".

00:16:45.649 --> 00:16:49.870
It’s part of the last-minute backup that
Site-01 performed as part of Stage 3 Containment

00:16:49.870 --> 00:16:51.230
Breach Protocols.

00:16:51.230 --> 00:16:55.339
If anyone asks where those backups are stored,
you can tell them the same thing I told you

00:16:55.339 --> 00:16:58.399
– it’s beyond their clearance.

00:16:58.399 --> 00:17:02.760
-The Administrator"
O5-1 was present in the O5 Council Conference

00:17:02.760 --> 00:17:03.760
Room.

00:17:03.760 --> 00:17:07.480
He was working at a laptop in front of him,
beside which sat a cup of coffee.

00:17:07.480 --> 00:17:11.030
A message flashed up on the screen, reading:
Access Granted.

00:17:11.030 --> 00:17:14.780
You have five minutes to complete an action
before the session automatically shuts down.

00:17:14.780 --> 00:17:17.200
He grumbled to himself, irritated.

00:17:17.200 --> 00:17:22.521
Two minutes passed before the remaining council
members except for O5-13 entered the room.

00:17:22.521 --> 00:17:23.521
O5-1: You're all here!

00:17:23.521 --> 00:17:25.710
Great, wouldn't want one of you to be off-site
for this.

00:17:25.710 --> 00:17:27.530
O5-4: One, what’s this about?

00:17:27.530 --> 00:17:31.260
I know you’ve been going through a phase
lately, but emergency meetings demand a real

00:17:31.260 --> 00:17:32.260
emergency.

00:17:32.260 --> 00:17:33.260
O5-1: Oh, it’s an emergency alright.

00:17:33.260 --> 00:17:34.890
O5-8: Then spit it out.

00:17:34.890 --> 00:17:35.890
We have a breach?

00:17:35.890 --> 00:17:36.940
New XK level threat?

00:17:36.940 --> 00:17:40.120
O5-1: No, it’s more of something under Two’s
jurisdiction.

00:17:40.120 --> 00:17:42.720
We have an internal affairs issue.

00:17:42.720 --> 00:17:44.320
O5-1 motioned to the coffee.

00:17:44.320 --> 00:17:48.040
O5-1: One of you bastards thought I would
actually drink this.

00:17:48.040 --> 00:17:50.410
O5-11: Someone didn’t give you enough sugar?

00:17:50.410 --> 00:17:53.090
O5-1: No, too much arsenic.

00:17:53.090 --> 00:17:56.510
Another message flashed up on the computer,
reading: You have three minutes to complete

00:17:56.510 --> 00:17:59.230
an action before the session automatically
shuts down.

00:17:59.230 --> 00:18:01.020
O5-8: Do you want to finish with that?

00:18:01.020 --> 00:18:02.880
O5-1: That pain-in-the-ass can be patient.

00:18:02.880 --> 00:18:04.560
O5-4: Wait, wait.

00:18:04.560 --> 00:18:08.050
You think one of us tried to kill you with
your… coffee.

00:18:08.050 --> 00:18:11.220
O5-1: Oh, don’t act like that’s below
you.

00:18:11.220 --> 00:18:13.160
I know you’ve all been out to bury my ass.

00:18:13.160 --> 00:18:14.740
O5-5: One, calm down.

00:18:14.740 --> 00:18:17.100
I know we’ve had our differences but—
O5-1: But what?

00:18:17.100 --> 00:18:20.010
It’s not like this is the first time one
of you has tried to destroy me.

00:18:20.010 --> 00:18:23.280
I know your guys once tried to infiltrate
one of my transports.

00:18:23.280 --> 00:18:24.280
O5-5: Infiltrate?

00:18:24.280 --> 00:18:27.000
He was assigned to fill in for—
O5-7: It’s no use, Five.

00:18:27.000 --> 00:18:28.700
The man can't think straight anymore.

00:18:28.700 --> 00:18:30.260
O5-1: Oh really?

00:18:30.260 --> 00:18:34.710
Who’s the one here with his head so far
up Marshall’s ass he can taste the caviar?

00:18:34.710 --> 00:18:37.620
O5-7: You’re accusing me of selling out?

00:18:37.620 --> 00:18:38.790
O5-1: No, no.

00:18:38.790 --> 00:18:43.780
I’m accusing all of you of selling out,
or being out for yourself or some nonsense.

00:18:43.780 --> 00:18:45.530
You’ve all gone soft.

00:18:45.530 --> 00:18:48.320
It used to be ”if it don’t make sense,
throw it in a cage”.

00:18:48.320 --> 00:18:51.250
Now it's “let’s measure it, look into
it, figure out what we know, then make sure

00:18:51.250 --> 00:18:52.460
it doesn’t bother anyone”.

00:18:52.460 --> 00:18:54.040
That’s not containment.

00:18:54.040 --> 00:18:57.610
That’s sitting idly and hoping the public
doesn’t find it.

00:18:57.610 --> 00:19:00.440
My god, we’ve started outsourcing to pet
shelters!

00:19:00.440 --> 00:19:05.070
O5-4: You know, if this is a problem we can
just calm down and rethink our stances on

00:19:05.070 --> 00:19:06.250
a few things.

00:19:06.250 --> 00:19:08.200
O5-1: That won’t change anything.

00:19:08.200 --> 00:19:11.410
Half of you are under someone’s thumb and
the other half of you are so messed up you

00:19:11.410 --> 00:19:12.580
need a cell of your own.

00:19:12.580 --> 00:19:15.480
O5-7: Says the man who suggested we drink
from the Fountain of Youth.

00:19:15.480 --> 00:19:17.450
O5-1: Well, Seven you’re right.

00:19:17.450 --> 00:19:20.420
I’m about as far from baseline as the rest
of you.

00:19:20.420 --> 00:19:22.640
Like, goddamn it, anomalies are essentially
running this organization.

00:19:22.640 --> 00:19:23.640
Ten’s learned how to do magic from the library.

00:19:23.640 --> 00:19:24.640
I need to take a whole cocktail of drugs just
to remember Eight exists.

00:19:24.640 --> 00:19:27.100
The computer chimed in again, saying: You
have two minutes to complete an action before

00:19:27.100 --> 00:19:28.710
the session automatically shuts down.

00:19:28.710 --> 00:19:30.470
O5-1: [to the computer] Shut up goddamn it!

00:19:30.470 --> 00:19:32.020
O5-10: We're getting off topic.

00:19:32.020 --> 00:19:33.260
You said someone poisoned you.

00:19:33.260 --> 00:19:34.260
What about Thirteen?

00:19:34.260 --> 00:19:35.260
He’s not even here!

00:19:35.260 --> 00:19:37.900
O5-1: That’s because I sent him to talk
to Nobody.

00:19:37.900 --> 00:19:39.200
O5-10: Why?

00:19:39.200 --> 00:19:42.040
O5-1: Because he’s the only one I trust.

00:19:42.040 --> 00:19:44.640
He’s the only one I don’t need to have
this chat with.

00:19:44.640 --> 00:19:47.540
He’s the only normal person on this whole
god damn Council.

00:19:47.540 --> 00:19:50.940
We plucked him off the streets, and just started
asking him “do you think this is weird?”

00:19:50.940 --> 00:19:54.110
I’m not worried about someone whose movements
we’ve been able to monitor since he came

00:19:54.110 --> 00:19:55.530
out of the uterus.

00:19:55.530 --> 00:19:59.800
You freaks— I don’t know what you all
did before you showed up here.

00:19:59.800 --> 00:20:03.560
For all I know you’re just eldritch abominations
waiting for the chance to kill me dead.

00:20:03.560 --> 00:20:05.000
O5-4: One, slow down.

00:20:05.000 --> 00:20:09.191
They were so wrapped up in their argument,
they barely noticed the computer saying: You

00:20:09.191 --> 00:20:13.310
have one minute to complete an action before
the session automatically shuts down.

00:20:13.310 --> 00:20:14.720
O5-1: And you know what?

00:20:14.720 --> 00:20:18.180
We’ve always been pretty liberal with containing
anomalies.

00:20:18.180 --> 00:20:20.360
Now we might have twelve of them on the Council.

00:20:20.360 --> 00:20:21.360
O5-12: One!

00:20:21.360 --> 00:20:22.360
O5-1: What?

00:20:22.360 --> 00:20:23.360
O5-12: Your session!

00:20:23.360 --> 00:20:24.360
Just finish it already.

00:20:24.360 --> 00:20:25.360
It's distracting as all hell.

00:20:25.360 --> 00:20:26.760
O5-1: You know… you're right.

00:20:26.760 --> 00:20:28.300
I should just finish it already.

00:20:28.300 --> 00:20:30.390
There's not much more for me to do.

00:20:30.390 --> 00:20:32.720
O5-1 resumed his work at the computer.

00:20:32.720 --> 00:20:37.730
O5-1: Aside from containing you, like the
inhuman aberrations you are.

00:20:37.730 --> 00:20:39.950
But it was a little too late for that.

00:20:39.950 --> 00:20:44.510
The computer, which had been allowed to time
out, said: Emergency Stage 3 Containment Breach

00:20:44.510 --> 00:20:45.940
Protocol Activated.

00:20:45.940 --> 00:20:50.100
The on-site nuclear warhead will detonate
in 5…4…3…

00:20:50.100 --> 00:20:55.670
This concludes the file on SCP-001.

00:20:55.670 --> 00:20:59.910
It appears that, in a place dedicated to studying
the strange and unusual, where the bizarre

00:20:59.910 --> 00:21:04.580
and anomalous have become the pedestrian,
the usual, just another day at the office,

00:21:04.580 --> 00:21:07.930
the most notable thing a person can be...is
completely average.

00:21:07.930 --> 00:21:12.600
When the impossible becomes possible, when
you and everyone around you are the furthest

00:21:12.600 --> 00:21:16.890
thing from normal, the ordinary is the stuff
of nightmares.

00:21:16.890 --> 00:21:23.460
Now go check out “SCP-001 Does Not Exist"
and “SCP-001 - A Simple Toymaker” for

00:21:23.460 --> 00:21:26.800
more proposals pertaining to the endless mysteries
of SCP-001.

